virtual dom?
React creates a virtual DOM — it's just a copy of the real DOM in memory.
When the data (state/props) changes, React:creates a new virtual DOM first .Compares the new virtual DOM with the old one (called "diffing")
React then updates only the changed parts in the real DOM — not the whole page.
jbv koi action (like click, input, etc.) hota to new virtual dom bnta.
->“Reconciliation is the process where React compares Virtual DOM with Real DOM and updates only the changed elements.”

